messages.reasoning_content:
SqlCollation.IMPLICIT doesn't mark quoted. `isComponentQuoted` probably checks component positions? Not worth.

### Test 20: validated node type storage
```
SqlIdentifier id = new SqlIdentifier("Q", pos);
assertNull(v.getValidatedNodeTypeIfKnown(id));
CalciteContextException e = assertThrows(... v.getValidatedNodeType(id));
contains "Unknown identifier 'Q'"
v.setValidatedNodeType(id, tf.createSqlType(INTEGER));
assertEquals(INTEGER, v.getValidatedNodeType(id).getSqlTypeName());
v.removeValidatedNodeType(id);
assertNull(v.getValidatedNodeTypeIfKnown(id));
```
And unknown type not stored:
```
v.setValidatedNodeType(id, v.getUnknownType());
assertNull(v.getValidatedNodeTypeIfKnown(id));
```
`getUnknownType()` returns nullable unknown; set ignores equality.

### Test 21: operand types
```
SqlCall call = (SqlCall) ((SqlSelect) parse("SELECT ABS(-1)")).getSelectList().get(0);
assertNull(v.getValidatedOperandTypes(call));
List<RelDataType> types = Arrays.asList(tf.createSqlType(INTEGER), tf.createSqlType(VARCHAR, 5));
v.callToOperandTypesMap.put(call, types);
assertEquals(types, v.getValidatedOperandTypes(call));
```
But field is declared `public final IdentityHashMap<SqlCall, List<RelDataType>>`; accessible. Good.

### Test 22: parameter row type + validateParameterizedExpression
```
SqlNode q = parse("SELECT CAST(? AS INTEGER), CAST(? AS VARCHAR(5))");
SqlNode validated = v.validateParameterizedExpression(q, Collections.emptyMap());
RelDataType paramType = v.getParameterRowType(validated);
assertEquals(2, paramType.getFieldCount());
